{
  "about": "Where each of Heliox's folders is, per system: config, data and state (\"heliox-os\" under $XDG_CONFIG_HOME, $XDG_DATA_HOME, $XDG_STATE_HOME when the value, blanks removed, is an absolute path, else under ~/.config, ~/.local/share, ~/.local/state), runtime (token files and port lock), cache (~/.cache/heliox) and setup (~/.config/heliox-os). Read by daemon/tests/test_heliox_folders_cases.py (pilot.config) and by the Rust test in tauri-app/src-tauri/src/folders.rs, so the app and the daemon cannot drift apart. A case checks the folders named in its expected map. {root} is C: on Windows and empty elsewhere, so a set value is an absolute path on the machine running the test (both sides check that, as the XDG specification says). run_user_writable: /run/user/<uid> exists and this user may write it. Paths use forward slashes; both tests compare with forward slashes.",
